WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.420
Posts, charts and ads that get a real response.

2
00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:08.980
This is the video for module 2 of Content Creation with Canva and Phone Tools.

3
00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:15.180
People scroll fast. Your post has about one thumb movement to make someone stop.

4
00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:20.690
So the image and first caption line must be clear on a small screen.

5
00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:24.180
You will also make charts that tell the truth.

6
00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:27.950
And small ads that bring real messages.

7
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:35.560
One message per post. A post about your new braiding style should not also announce your church programme.

8
00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:42.420
A hook in large text, five to eight words, like Knotless braids, ready in 4 hours.

9
00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:54.890
A real photo of your work. Real work builds trust faster than stock photos. Portrait posts at 1080 by 1350 fill more of the screen.

10
00:00:56.140 --> 00:01:00.300
Your brand colours, and a small logo in the same corner every time.

11
00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:06.900
And a call to action. What should she do now? Send a DM to book, or WhatsApp your number.

12
00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:17.200
For example, Hauwa makes whipped shea butter in Kaduna. Only the first lines of a caption show before more, so she puts the important words first.

13
00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:21.480
Her hook: Dry skin this harmattan? This is for you.

14
00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:30.260
The value: only shea butter and coconut oil, a 250 g jar, about 3,500 naira.

15
00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:36.970
The proof: over 40 jars sent out this month. She counted her own orders, so it is true.

16
00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:47.200
The action: WhatsApp to order, with delivery within Kaduna. Price, size and how to order are the three questions customers ask most.

17
00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:56.050
Never claim a product cures a disease, or is NAFDAC approved, unless it has a real NAFDAC registration number.

18
00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:08.800
First write your one main message, and list the facts that support it, using only numbers you can check. Then choose the chart. A bar chart compares amounts across a few groups.

19
00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:12.240
A line chart shows change over time.

20
00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:17.850
A pie chart shows parts of one whole, with 4 to 5 slices at most.

21
00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:23.830
In Canva, search Elements for Charts, then type your labels and values into the small table.

22
00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:35.420
Here is a worked example. Grace wants one image for the end-of-year meeting. Her message: together we saved more than ever. Members grew from 12 to 30.

23
00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:44.570
From the record book, the group saved 360,000 naira in the first quarter, and 540,000 in the second.

24
00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:54.410
Then 810,000 in the third quarter, and 900,000 in the fourth. These are illustrative figures for the example.

25
00:02:55.660 --> 00:03:07.400
She adds them up herself before designing: 2,610,000 naira. Then she builds the bar chart, labels the axis Naira saved, and adds the source at the bottom.

26
00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:21.510
Charts can mislead, even by accident. A bar chart that does not start at zero makes small differences look huge. Missing units leave people guessing whether it is naira, people or percentages.

27
00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:28.520
Run these five checks, then send the image to yourself on WhatsApp and check every word can be read without zooming.

28
00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:45.060
For example, Kemi sells phone chargers in Computer Village, Ikeja. Her story is 1080 by 1920, with text kept out of the top and bottom 250 pixels, where the name and reply box cover it.

29
00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:53.740
She makes two versions. Version A says fast chargers. Version B says original chargers, tested in front of you.

30
00:03:54.990 --> 00:04:00.810
She boosts each one for 3 days, at the same small daily budget, to people around Lagos.

31
00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:09.440
Then she counts real chats. Version A brought 9, and version B brought 21, in her own illustrative count.

32
00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:16.520
She keeps version B. Customers cared more about the charger being genuine than about speed.

33
00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:23.080
Divide the money spent by the number of sales. If an ad costs more per sale than your profit, stop it.

34
00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:33.950
And beware of ad scams. Ignore messages saying your page will be deleted unless you click a link. Manage ads only inside the official apps.

35
00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:47.780
To remember. One message and one call to action. Hook, Value, Proof, Action, with only true claims. Honest charts. Story text in the safe zone. And test small before spending more.

36
00:04:49.030 --> 00:05:00.830
Your turn. Design a five-slide carousel with a caption. Make an honest infographic. Refresh your banner or CV. And make an animated story, with a short written ad plan.

37
00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:03.120
Continue with the lessons below.
